      "id": 16060,
      "name": "McBehrer",
      "username": "McBehrer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-01-12T21:12:06.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So, I was playing against The Matriarch, with Parse on my team, in Zhu Long's temple. I had Updated intel in play, and when Matriarch played a Fowl Card, I revealed the bottom card of the environment deck. It was a Shinobi, which was forced into play, killing the Fowl.</p><p>Contrary to my expectations, though, Matriarch did not continue playing cards. That was just the end of her turn.</p><p>It was my understanding that killing a bird as it entered play did not prevent her from playing another one; after all, the Hairtrigger Reflexes exploit was the main reason the \"play the top card of the villain deck\" text was moved from the birds to the Matriarch character card itself. So even if the bird is killed, it still entered play, so she should still play another card. So why, then, did this particular combination cut off her turn? I'd say, probably a bug.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, incidentally, I didn't get to look at the NEXT bottom card of the environment deck, either. I expect that's probably working as intended, but I'm not sure, since the Shinobis' behavior was recently changed.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:48:39.414Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
